{"challenge_axes":[],"difficulty":4,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.2.0","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","record_hash":"2d72c7664975ebebc4e0ce511b92a7c701d0e71621b7110a5f8827f2b42f699d","rendered_input":"Graph contract: kind=graph. nodes contains distinct strings. edges contains [from,to,cost] triples with positive integer fuel costs and at most one edge per ordered pair. start and goal are nodes; fuel is a nonnegative integer. plan is an ordered list of destination node names. Every edge is directed. Start at {node:start,fuel:fuel}. An action is legal exactly when an edge from the current node to its destination exists and its cost is at most the remaining fuel. A legal move changes node to its destination and subtracts the edge cost. At the first illegal action, include that action's {legal:false,after:unchanged_state} step, stop immediately, and do not evaluate subsequent actions. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed action was legal. reaches_goal is true exactly when the whole plan is valid and its terminal node is goal, including an initially satisfied goal with an empty plan. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL state that reaches goal within initial fuel, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the entire destination-name sequence. It is [] for an initially satisfied goal and null if no feasible plan exists. Fuel cost is a feasibility constraint, not the optimization objective. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:{node:string,fuel:integer}}], after:{node:string,fuel:integer}, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"plan\":[\"Aster\",\"Fjord\",\"Aster\",\"Fjord\",\"Aster\",\"Fjord\",\"Aster\",\"Fjord\",\"Aster\",\"Fjord\",\"Ember\"],\"fuel\":4,\"goal\":\"Ember\",\"start\":\"Fjord\",\"edges\":[[\"Fjord\",\"Aster\",2],[\"Aster\",\"Ember\",2],[\"Aster\",\"Fjord\",1]],\"nodes\":[\"Fjord